    {
      "id": "dt-step-1",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "1. Name it",
      "position": {
        "x": -1080,
        "y": 20
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 360,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "position": {
            "side": "top",
            "offset": 0.2
          }
        }
      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "position": {
            "side": "top",
            "offset": 0.2
          },
          "portId": "root"
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "declaration-template"
        },
        "title": "1. Name it",
        "body": "Open the Declaration's editor and fill in the Identity tab: a name people will recognize, a version, and a one-sentence description. The description shows on cards and in lists, so write it for someone who has never seen the graph.\n\nThe graph's id is made for you and must stay the same for the life of the graph, because other graphs find yours by it. Rename the graph freely. Never change its id.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          }
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/templates/page-template/classes/page-section.node-class.node"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "dt-step-2",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "2. Say what it is",
      "position": {
        "x": -420,
        "y": 20
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 360,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "position": {
            "side": "top",
            "offset": 0.2
          }
        }
      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "position": {
            "side": "top",
            "offset": 0.2
          },
          "portId": "root"
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "declaration-template"
        },
        "title": "2. Say what it is",
        "body": "Choose the kind of graph: a plan, a note, a contract, a task board, a template. The kind belongs on the Declaration, never in a title node or a field. It tells people, and tools, how to treat the graph.\n\nKeep the scope honest too: local for your own work, shared for something others will build on.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          }
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/templates/page-template/classes/page-section.node-class.node"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "dt-step-3",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "3. Give it a face",
      "position": {
        "x": 240,
        "y": 20
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 360,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "position": {
            "side": "top",
            "offset": 0.2
          }
        }
      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "position": {
            "side": "top",
            "offset": 0.2
          },
          "portId": "root"
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "declaration-template"
        },
        "title": "3. Give it a face",
        "body": "A graph presents itself through a Surface: a chain of Views, richest first, ending in a Glyph. Drag from the surface handle on the Declaration to make the first View. Drag from that View's next-view handle to add a smaller one. Add a Glyph last and connect it, so the chain ends in a mark that still reads at a tiny size.\n\nOne View is enough to begin. Twilite shows the richest View that fits the room it has, and the Glyph when there is almost none. This page is exactly that: a page, a summary card, an icon, then a glyph.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          }
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/templates/page-template/classes/page-section.node-class.node"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "dt-step-4",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "4. Choose where it lands",
      "position": {
        "x": -1080,
        "y": 460
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 360,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "position": {
            "side": "top",
            "offset": 0.2
          }
        }
      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "position": {
            "side": "top",
            "offset": 0.2
          },
          "portId": "root"
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "declaration-template"
        },
        "title": "4. Choose where it lands",
        "body": "Every graph has one landing surface: the node a visitor sees first. Drag from the landing surface handle to create it.\n\nIts distance and direction from the Declaration also set the graph's frame, the shape it takes as a card in a workspace. Size it so everything that should stay visible is inside the frame.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          }
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/templates/page-template/classes/page-section.node-class.node"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "dt-step-5",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "5. Decide what you share",
      "position": {
        "x": -420,
        "y": 460
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 360,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "position": {
            "side": "top",
            "offset": 0.2
          }
        }
      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "position": {
            "side": "top",
            "offset": 0.2
          },
          "portId": "root"
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "declaration-template"
        },
        "title": "5. Decide what you share",
        "body": "Ports are optional named entry points that other graphs can use. Leave them out until you need one.\n\nBridges bring in the node classes you build with (imports, down the left of this graph) and offer yours to others (exports, top right). Authority says who may create, change or delete: people, agents, tools. Anything not granted is not allowed.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          }
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/templates/page-template/classes/page-section.node-class.node"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "dt-step-6",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "6. Lay it out",
      "position": {
        "x": 240,
        "y": 460
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 360,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "position": {
            "side": "top",
            "offset": 0.2
          }
        }
      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "position": {
            "side": "top",
            "offset": 0.2
          },
          "portId": "root"
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "declaration-template"
        },
        "title": "6. Lay it out",
        "body": "Put each kind of node in its own place so the graph reads at a glance. The Declaration goes top left. Import bridges run down the left side. Export bridges take the top half of the right side and portals the bottom half. Views run along the bottom, and everything else stays inside that boundary.\n\nLook at this graph: that is where everything is. An empty region is fine. The layout is about where things sit, not about filling every corner.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          }
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/templates/page-template/classes/page-section.node-class.node"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "dt-step-7",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "7. Check it",
      "position": {
        "x": -1080,
        "y": 900
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 360,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "position": {
            "side": "top",
            "offset": 0.2
          }
        }
      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "position": {
            "side": "top",
            "offset": 0.2
          },
          "portId": "root"
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "declaration-template"
        },
        "title": "7. Check it",
        "body": "Open the graph and look for warnings. A missing landing surface, a Surface that does not end in a Glyph, and two Surfaces with the same id are all reported, and each names the node to fix.\n\nThen save, close and reopen it. A graph that looks the same after reloading is sound.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          }
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/templates/page-template/classes/page-section.node-class.node"
      }
    },
